{
  "id": "verb-position-2",
  "name": "Present tense: -ir and -re verbs (finir, vendre)",
  "level": "A1",
  "variety": "fr-FR",
  "subtitle": "Two more groups of regular verbs. -ir verbs like finir add -iss- in the plural: je finis, nous finissons. -re verbs like vendre, attendre and répondre have no ending in the il form: je vends, il vend.",
  "briefMarks": ["finir", "finis", "finit", "finissons", "vendre", "vends"],
  "source": "icanspeak French original text (grammar-a1 run, 2026-11-08)",
  "status": "entwurf",
  "concept": {
    "flow": [
      { "text": "-ir: finis, finit, finissons", "variant": "prep" },
      { "text": "-re: vends, vend, vendons", "variant": "verb" }
    ],
    "exampleHtml": "<span class=\"vp-prep\">Je finis</span> à cinq heures. · <span class=\"vp-prep\">Nous choisissons</span> un menu. · <span class=\"vp-verb\">Il vend</span> du pain. · <span class=\"vp-verb\">Vous attendez</span> le bus<em> ?</em>",
    "qa": [
      {
        "html": "<strong>-ir verbs like finir</strong>: <em>finis, finis, finit, finissons, finissez, finissent</em>. In the plural you add <strong>-iss-</strong>. Others: <em>choisir, remplir, réussir, grandir</em>.",
        "tag": "-ir: finir"
      },
      {
        "html": "In speech, <em>je finis, tu finis, il finit</em> sound the same. But the plural is easy to hear: <em>nous finissons, ils finissent</em> have the sound “iss”. So <em>il finit</em> and <em>ils finissent</em> sound different.",
        "tag": "Hear the plural"
      },
      {
        "html": "<strong>-re verbs like vendre</strong>: <em>vends, vends, vend, vendons, vendez, vendent</em>. The <em>il</em> form has no ending. Others: <em>attendre, répondre, entendre, perdre, descendre</em>.",
        "tag": "-re: vendre"
      },
      {
        "html": "Note the <em>d</em>: it is silent in <em>il vend</em> but you hear it in <em>ils vendent</em> and <em>nous vendons</em>.",
        "tag": "il vend / ils vendent"
      },
      {
        "html": "<strong>attendre</strong> means “to wait for” and takes no preposition: <em>J'attends le bus. Elle attend Camille.</em> <strong>répondre</strong> takes <em>à</em>: <em>Je réponds au téléphone.</em>",
        "tag": "attendre, répondre"
      },
      {
        "html": "Not every verb in <em>-ir</em> is like <em>finir</em>. <em>partir, venir, dormir, ouvrir</em> follow other patterns: <em>je pars, je viens, je dors, j'ouvre</em>. At A1, learn them one by one.",
        "tag": "Careful"
      }
    ],
    "noteHtml": "Common mistakes: ✗ <em>Je finit</em> → ✓ <em>Je finis</em>. ✗ <em>Nous finons</em> → ✓ <em>Nous finissons</em>. ✗ <em>Il vends</em> → ✓ <em>Il vend</em>. ✗ <em>J'attends pour le bus</em> → ✓ <em>J'attends le bus</em>. Next: <a href=\"/present-irreguliers\">key irregular verbs</a> and <a href=\"/present-verbes-er\">the present of -er verbs</a>.",
    "reference": {
      "showLabel": "Show overview ▼",
      "hideLabel": "Hide overview ▲",
